  "notes": "ケア comes from English \"care\" and is used both as a noun and as a suru verb (ケアする).\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- スキンケア: skincare\n- ヘアケア: hair care\n- メンタルケア: mental health care\n- {介護|かいご}ケア: nursing care\n- アフターケア: aftercare, follow-up care\n- セルフケア: self-care\n- ケアマネージャー: care manager (in nursing/welfare)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {手入|てい}れ: maintenance, grooming (more traditional Japanese term)\n- {介護|かいご}: nursing care (specifically for elderly/disabled, more formal)\n- {世話|せわ}: taking care of, looking after (broader, everyday term)",
